    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: bf7c0d068adaedd79a12721b0d618994447b4ed7 -->\nReviewer: uma pool job review-4442, GPT-6 (Codex), mkinney; did not write or refresh this PR.\n\nClean. Ready for the maintainer to merge at the next cut. No blocking findings.\n\nThis is a SAFETY-tier review because the change affects posted G-code. I read all five changed files and the issue and PR threads. The ready flag provides the author hand-off. No unreleased writer record was present.\n\nLocal trial merge:\n- PR head: `bf7c0d068adaedd79a12721b0d618994447b4ed7`.\n- Main: `b6089ea6e82c0bc47ebb6cf7343b5956684e1126`.\n- Trial merge: `2d7bafee3b32feb5ae2fe2aff60913eb93cbd5fd`. Its first parent is the PR head.\n- The merge was clean. All commands ran locally in `.claude/worktrees/review-4442`. No GitHub runner was used.\n\nWhat I checked:\n- The mode values, option-2 guard, tolerance limits, named refusals, and section reset agree with the stated scope.\n- I checked section 8.10, pages 509–511, of the [HEIDENHAIN manual](https://content.heidenhain.de/doku/tnc_guide/pdf_files/iTNC530/34049x-neu/en/bhb.pdf).\n- I read all 66 lines of the new `picomax_smoothing.nc` golden. The enable blocks precede motion. The reset precedes M9/M5. The next section has no smoothing blocks.\n- No existing golden changed. The PR body names the new golden and explains its output.\n- The tests join the existing suite. The decision file records the alternatives and the reset inference.\n\nLocal results:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 34 steps passed, one step skipped, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The suites passed 1,597 tests.\n- Post suites passed: lib (185), post_engine (143), script_arcs (49), script_cycles (122), script_dialects (175), script_edm (87), script_goldens (445), script_probe (39), script_rotary (66), script_wcs (108).\n- G-code `klartext`: 25 passed. App `conformance`: 7 passed. App `klartext_builtin`: 3 passed. All other app suites selected by the quick plan passed.\n- App `example_catalog`: 50 passed, 4 existing ignored tests. App `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`: 1 passed each.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps passed, 0 failed, 0 stalled. All 11 light tests passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 16 -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n\nExtra suites run:\n- `cargo test -j 16 -p camcraft-app --test smoothing`: 8 passed.\n- I searched for readers of the changed golden directory. The quick gate ran the post fixture suites and the G-code Klartext suite listed above.\n- The catalog suites ran by name within the quick gate. No importer code or STEP fixture changed.\n\nMutation checks:\n- Removed the `smoothOff()` call in a temporary copy: RED. The section-reset assertion detected the missing reset. Original script: GREEN.\n- Reversed the HSC finish/rough values in a temporary copy: RED. The rough-mode assertion detected the wrong word. Original script: GREEN.\n- The probes used the post CLI and the assertions from the new tests. All copies and output stayed under `/tmp`. The PR source stayed unchanged.\n\nLimits:\n- The site-test step was skipped because Node.js is absent. This is not a test pass.\n- No test ran on a real control. The empty-T reset block remains an inference from the documented NO ENT reset. The decision file states this limit.\n- No full heavy lane ran. Current main does not require it for this P6 change.\n\nRequested before merge: none.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
